INSERT INTO `quest_request_items` (`ID`, `EmoteOnComplete`, `EmoteOnIncomplete`, `CompletionText`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
(175013, 0, 0, 'Weakness is also a sin.', 0),
(175014, 0, 0, '<The dwarf crusader''s condition is serious.>', 0),
(175015, 0, 0, 'May the Light guide the crusaders wherever they are. Have you managed to find them?', 0),
(175016, 0, 0, '<Among piles of scrolls and books, Scholar Enharon watches you with one eye narrowed and an arched eyebrow.>$B$BWhat is the reason for your interruption?', 0),
(175017, 0, 0, '<The prayer recited by Father Amrod envelops his presence in a cold light.>', 0),
(175023, 0, 0, '<Despite the common gesture of clenching his jaws, the tension running through the rest of the gnoll’s body reveals that he is no ordinary one.>', 0),
(175027, 0, 0, '<The elf''s gaze rests on some point upon the horizon, beyond the white peaks that cradle the valley.>', 0),
(175035, 0, 0, 'Gah...! Curse those Ealdir. It hurts like hell...', 0),
(175036, 0, 0, 'Well?', 0),
(175037, 0, 0, 'I am still waiting for that show. Or are you all talk?', 0),
(175041, 0, 0, 'Is it done? Is my son... resting now?', 0),
(175042, 0, 0, 'Please... grant them all rest.', 0),
(175043, 0, 0, '<The creature''s gaze rests upon a point infinitely far away.>', 0),
(175044, 0, 0, '<Aisling seems to be resting her throat between songs. She is the bard of this inn, if appearances can be trusted.>', 0),
(175045, 0, 0, 'What? Do we have a problem, you and I?', 0),
(175047, 0, 0, 'Can I assume the area is safe once more?', 0),
(175051, 0, 0, '<The lieutenant is deep in thought, studying the troll ruins, and remains unaware of your presence.>', 0),
(175052, 0, 0, 'Did that help you get it off your chest?', 0),
(175056, 0, 0, 'The fire, much like the wounded, requires tending.', 0),
(175057, 0, 0, 'Have you killed that monster?', 0),
(175066, 0, 0, 'One never forgets their first flight...', 0),
(175068, 0, 0, 'The murlocs took Dorothy...', 0),
(175069, 0, 0, 'I still hold onto hope that nothing irreparable has happened to my poor girl... Help me.', 0),
(175070, 0, 0, 'It had to be the kobolds who took Dorothy...', 0),
(175071, 0, 0, '<Ralda has a vacant stare.>', 0),
(175072, 0, 0, '<Rothfuss watches you without a word, steady but visibly weary.>', 0),
(175074, 0, 0, 'If it were up to me to determine the value of things, a bucket of fresh Windswept milk would be worth more than one filled with gold.', 0),
(175075, 0, 0, 'The clouds that break against the mountains of Scadeald create the perfect conditions for the mold to grow.', 0),
(175077, 0, 0, 'The pack alpha dictates the behavior of all the rest.', 0),
(175078, 0, 0, 'Yes?', 0),
(175079, 0, 0, '<The Commander is far too busy barking orders and coordinating the defense.>', 0),
(175080, 0, 0, 'Soldier?', 0),
(175082, 0, 0, 'Did you have a good time on the hunt? To be honest, I find little joy in it myself.', 0),
(175084, 0, 0, 'You''ve come from speaking with the High Elves, I see.', 0),
(175085, 0, 0, 'Are you finished with them?', 0),
(175086, 0, 0, 'Sh...', 0),
(175087, 0, 0, 'Arendor sent you, didn''t he?', 0),
(175089, 0, 0, 'Is it done? I hope you left a few for me.', 0),
(175091, 0, 0, '<The dwarf has been hiding here for hours. His face, with wide eyes and a feverish gaze, bears witness to his exhaustion.>', 0),
(175092, 0, 0, 'Have you managed to find anything out?', 0),
(175097, 0, 0, 'Has the debt been paid? Does the forest still bleed?', 0),
(175098, 0, 0, 'The Dryads are fading... have you managed to mend their spirits?', 0),
(175100, 0, 0, 'They... they were everywhere...', 0),
(175101, 0, 0, 'Is it done? Is the air thick with the scent of their failure?', 0),
(175102, 0, 0, 'Is the shadow finally lifted from this place?', 0),
(175103, 0, 0, '<Alto Bilberg sniffs you.>$B$BMedicine? You… bring medicine? Much time has passed!', 0),
(175104, 0, 0, 'Were you able to find any?', 0),
(175105, 0, 0, 'Has everyone been fed? I hope the bread brought them some comfort.', 0),
(175106, 0, 0, 'Tell me the job is done.', 0),
(175108, 0, 0, 'Stay back!', 0),
(175109, 0, 0, 'Is it... Is it safe to leave now?', 0),
(175112, 0, 0, 'How is the cull coming along?', 0),
(175113, 0, 0, 'Fond of fireworks, are you?', 0),
(175114, 0, 0, 'Has the bastard ceased to breathe?', 0),
(175115, 0, 0, 'Have you recovered the stones yet?', 0),
(175116, 0, 0, 'Bagga Darma must die.', 0),
(175121, 0, 0, '<The last cook of Coldmere Keep is too absorbed in his duties to notice your intrusion into his kitchen.>', 0),
(175122, 0, 0, 'What have we here? Ah, my refreshment. Most kind.', 0),
(175123, 0, 0, '<Lady Serenya Coldmere watches you. Her gaze is emptier than before...>', 0),
(175126, 0, 0, 'Do you hear the voices? The spirits of all those who were sacrificed... I will never forget how desperately they clung to this world, trying to escape the jaws of the Rooted Shadow.', 0),
(175128, 0, 0, 'What news do you bring?', 0),
(175129, 0, 0, 'Yes, what’s going on?', 0),
(175139, 0, 0, 'Alerts, alerts, and more alerts! What is happening out there?', 0),
(175140, 0, 0, 'WARNING! WARNING!', 0),
(175141, 0, 0, 'WARNING! DANGER!', 0),
(175142, 0, 0, 'WARNING! COLLECT!', 0),
(175143, 0, 0, 'WARNING! KILL!', 0),
(175144, 0, 0, 'What happened back there at Metantenna Station?', 0),
(175145, 0, 0, 'The Dark Irons have never been good neighbors, but their quarrel is with Ironforge. They care little for this city.$B$B<A fierce grimace spreads across the dwarf''s face.>$B$BNaudin Screwdriver has gone mad if he thinks I''ll send soldiers to aid him. Neither the Metantenna Station nor the Tram are our responsibility. He mistakes generosity for duty. Let him beg the Alliance for help!$B$BWe want no part in this war with the Dark Irons.', 0),
(175146, 0, 0, 'Finally!', 0),
(175147, 0, 0, 'Are they dead, then?', 0),
(175148, 0, 0, 'Did you find any? Did those trolls leave even a single egg intact?', 0),
(175149, 0, 0, 'Hold it right there.', 0),
(175150, 0, 0, 'Is the deed done?', 0),
(175151, 0, 0, 'I''m sorry to have tasked you with such a thing.', 0),
(175152, 0, 0, 'These... insects!', 0),
(175153, 0, 0, 'Incense? A pittance of an offering for one whose favor you seek.', 0),
(175155, 0, 0, 'Satisfied?', 0),
(175156, 0, 0, 'Hm...', 0),
(175157, 0, 0, 'Is the deed done? Have you sustained any injuries?', 0),
(175158, 0, 0, 'How many have fallen? Did they answer to a name?', 0),
(175159, 0, 0, 'Praise the Light.', 0),
(175160, 0, 0, 'You have returned.', 0),
(175161, 0, 0, 'The coals are ready! Do you have the meat?', 0),
(175162, 0, 0, 'As if I didn''t have enough problems already!', 0),
(175163, 0, 0, 'Don''t underestimate a part''s appearance, no matter how old or rusted it may be: if it fits into place... it''s the perfect part!', 0),
(175164, 0, 0, '<Commander Moore gives you a respectful nod, awaiting your words.>', 0),
(175167, 0, 0, 'Do you have any insights for me?', 0),
(175168, 0, 0, 'Very well.', 0),
(175169, 0, 0, 'Good.', 0),
(175170, 0, 0, 'Are you finished?', 0),
(175171, 0, 0, 'Ready?', 0),
(175172, 0, 0, 'Violence is written across your face. What have you discovered, my child?', 0),
(175173, 0, 0, 'Violence is a curious thing: at its root, it is an expression of chaos; and yet, Order can be imposed through it.', 0),
(175176, 0, 0, 'Your body is barely radiating any heat. Be careful; death by cold is a treacherous thing.', 0),
(175178, 0, 0, 'You have returned. We were waiting for you.', 0),
(175179, 0, 0, 'Yes?', 0),
(175180, 0, 0, 'Yes?', 0),
(175199, 0, 0, 'What have you brought me?', 0),
(175204, 0, 0, 'Treacherous Scadeald... A single whisper was enough to twist a grieving man''s love into something terrible and dangerous.', 0),
(175206, 0, 0, 'Do you have the cheese assortment?', 0);
INSERT INTO `quest_offer_reward` (`ID`, `Emote1`, `Emote2`, `Emote3`, `Emote4`, `EmoteDelay1`, `EmoteDelay2`, `EmoteDelay3`, `EmoteDelay4`, `RewardText`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
(175064, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'How much meat did you manage to get?$B$B<Bromli takes a quick glance.>$B$BGood, good. This will do for an appetizer. Yes, an ''appetizer''. Don''t look at me like that: I told you they eat more than you can imagine!', 0),
(175065, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Spotless, just the way I like ''em! How else are they supposed to rest? Besides, who''d want to lay eggs in a filthy nest?$B$BBetween you and me, it''s always given me a bit of a turn that they have the head of an eagle, the body of a lion, and... yet... they still lay eggs.', 0),
(175066, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Quite the experience, eh?$B$BThe wind in your face. The mountain chill. The landscape of Scadeald stretching out below...$B$BAh! No need to thank me. This is the least I could offer in exchange for the work you''ve done.$B$BIf the road ever brings you back to Daumor Peak, please, stop by and say hello.', 0),
(175075, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Yes, this should be enough to keep the cheese production going for quite some time.$B$BThank you.', 0),
(175082, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Ketheric feels the meat with a silly, hungry grin.>$B$BThis will be enough. Yes. I''ll see to the preparation of the meat myself.$B$BEvery soldier shall have their ration. And they''ll know exactly who to thank.', 0),
(175086, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Arendor presses a finger to his lips, using his other hand to signal for you to remain calm.>$B$BYou''ve already caused enough of a racket just getting here.', 0),
(175087, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I see... Well done. Late, by the way; but better late than never.$B$BWhat matters is that you''re here.', 0),
(175097, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Do you feel that? The breeze falling from the peaks, whispering through the trees. The melody of the river as it flows downstream. The song of the birds.$B$BThe forest speaks with a chorus of voices and sounds. And in every one of them, it thanks you.', 0),
(175104, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Do you feel it? Though subtle, each pinecone pulses like a heart with the latent magic of the forest.$B$BIt requires patience, care, and a great deal of finesse to extract the magic they hold within.$B$BGive me a moment and I shall show you.', 0),
(175105, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You have my gratitude, and that of the sanctuary.$B$BPlease, accept this as compensation for your trouble. And depart with the certainty that you will always be welcome in Namarien Sanctuary.', 0),
(175108, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You''re not one of them... Spirits be praised!$B$BWe''re all that''s left; those of us quick enough to slip through the Ealdir''s fingers.$B$BIs it... Is it safe to leave now?', 0),
(175112, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I hope you''ve sent a few of those ugly heads rolling.$B$BGood. The Ealdir will learn to fear you, if they don''t already.', 0),
(175113, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'We heard the blast from here. You can still see the smoke rising through the trees.$B$BFine work.', 0),
(175122, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Lady Serenya takes a timid sip from the wine glass. She frowns. She gives you a strange look. She brings the rim of the glass to her lips once more and drains the contents in one long draught.>$B$B<Her eyes, though hidden behind her veil, seem to cast a defiant gaze upon you.>', 0),
(175126, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The Great Mother is dead.$B$B<Deirdre''s voice takes on a strange cast as she declares Morgwena''s death. Perhaps she celebrates it. Or perhaps she is hiding regret.>$B$BAnd not soon enough.$B$BMorgwena leaves a bitter legacy, but without her shadow looming over us, we Ealdir will discover a kind of freedom we did not even know had been denied to us.$B$BAnd in the power vacuum that follows...', 0),
(175127, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<An unmoving corpse, sprawled along the shoreline. Gulls have pecked at his eyes, leaving behind two empty, bloodied sockets.>$B$B<Here and there, the shredded clothing reveals bites, scratches, and something stranger still; wounds that resemble stabs.>', 0),
(175130, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'What have we here?$B$BCareful! <Alcarian takes a step back. He narrowly avoids injuring himself on the tip.>$B$BAnd you say you plucked this from a murloc? Hm... They looked like sea urchins, then? A most peculiar mutation.$B$BOn behalf of the Academy of Arcane Arts and Sciences, you have my thanks.', 0),
(175138, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'At last! At last, they send someone!$B$BI was about to lose my mind! If I haven''t lost it already, that is!', 0),
(175141, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<The chaotic flailing of its lever-like legs reminds you of... a happy dance. You decide to roll with that interpretation.>', 0),
(175142, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<The Alarm-o-Bot reacts by emitting a little jingle that sounds remarkably like a "victory" fanfare.>$B$B<Once it finishes, a small hatch opens in its chassis to store the components. You deposit the parts inside.>$B$BI CARRY! PART! VALUE!', 0),
(175143, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Perhaps it''s the oppressive red light that won''t stop flashing, or the constant screeching of its speakers, but you would swear the news of the Dark Iron''s death has made the Alarm-o-Bot happy.>', 0),
(175145, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Determination to settle all the region''s woes is reflected in Baugwolf''s gaze.>', 0),
(175146, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Reinforcements from Dun Kazad?$B$B<Erdruin''s hope fades as he sees you have arrived alone.>$B$BBetter than nothing, I suppose.$B$B<He gestures toward the interior of the building.>$B$BWhat you see is all that is left: the four of us and Hedgwin, our gryphon. He is wounded, by the way.$B$BThe trolls... they slaughtered everyone else.', 0),
(175157, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I have kept you in my prayers, child. Praise the Light for bringing you back hale and hearty.$B$BHave you put those blasphemers to death?$B$BGood. Very good. You have been the avatar of the Light''s retribution. Now, allow me to make you a vessel of its generosity.', 0),
(175160, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'So, the witch is dead.$B$B<The Patriarch''s voice is devoid of emotion. The gaze from his gray eyes is more akin to that of a notary than a spiritual guide.>$B$BTell me her name, if you please. I wish to record it. Our devotion to the Pantheon is expressed through more than mere prayer; there is no labor more sacred to us, his faithful, than to gather, organize, and share knowledge.', 0),
(175162, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'There isn''t a machine Norhi builds that doesn''t end up in smithereens. It''s all thanks to his god-awful system code!$B$BWhat good is a solid chassis if the program running it has the intelligence of a trogg with two cymbals?', 0),
(175163, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Do you have the parts? Yes? Good. I''ve just finished installing the program. With that and what you''ve brought, I''ll have the tank ready in a heartbeat.$B$BIronical, isn''t it? Scrapping the conflicts of the past just to keep the machinery of war grinding on.$B$BConflicts that repeat, spinning round and round... just like this rotary gyro-gnomic part!$B$B<The Mekgineer snaps the part into a slot in the tank where it is physically impossible for it to ever spin or rotate again.>', 0),
(175164, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Is this...?$B$B<The Commander''s eyes are cold and dark. Bushy eyebrows frame his suspicious gaze.>$B$BThe tank, then. And they''ve had you play the part of the messenger $gboy:girl;.$B$BI only hope this tank lasts longer than the last one.', 0),
(175166, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<The dwarf woman''s face is an unshakeable mask. Despite the grief clouding her eyes, she maintains a stony composure.>$B$BYou are not from Dun Kazad.$B$BI suppose my late husband inspired such admiration that folk from all corners come to honor him.$B$BYou are welcome here.', 0),
(175167, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You have spoken with them, then?$B$B<Bilna gazes into the horizon, lost in her thoughts. After a long moment, she comes to; her large eyes filled with sorrow.>$B$BLet your instincts guide you, and choose which of the two to favor.$B$BIn the meantime, I shall try to make my own peace with the decision.', 0),
(175168, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'And in the name of the Church, I accept your aid.$B$BThere is much work to be done here. With any luck, our labors may yet inspire poor Holdor''s widow to consecrate her husband''s spirit to the Light.', 0),
(175169, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Your readiness honors us all.$B$BLet us strive together, you and I, to bring luster to the memory of the champion Holdor, and comfort to his widow.', 0),
(175170, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Good. It is a start.', 0),
(175171, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You have restored Order to the cemetery.$B$BFor a time.$B$BSooner or later, as with all things, chaos will eventually reclaim it once more.', 0),
(175172, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Yetis? So close?$B$BPraise the Light for guiding your hand against those beasts. I understand the gravedigger now, and I am almost glad he neglected his duties!$B$BWho knows what the yetis would have done to him had they caught him...', 0),
(175173, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'It is great news that you have dealt with the yetis. But I must ask: did you learn anything about them? Any curiosities? Anything that set them apart from other tribes?$B$BSuch knowledge is of extreme value to the Creed of the Pantheon.$B$BAll Lore is sacred.', 0),
(175175, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Candle in hand, purple skin, chattering teeth... You''re here for the Brazier of Unity, aren''t you?$B$B<Enril shakes his head slowly, as if to himself.>$B$BI cannot help you, I''m afraid.', 0),
(175178, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Bilna''s glassy eyes light up, reflecting the flickering flame of the candle.>$B$BThe Candle of Unity. One of our most deep-rooted traditions. An honor like few others. This truly honors my husband.$B$BAnd as for the matter of faith...', 0),
(175179, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'It is done.$B$BMay the Light hold him in its glory, and may it grant solace to his kin.$B$BDeath is always harder on the living.', 0),
(175180, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Austere words, yet sincere.$B$BNow the true work begins: for to remember is to carry a burden, and while it provides comfort, it can also lead to exhaustion.$B$BThe Creed of the Pantheon will be here to guide them when they feel the weight of memory is about to crush them.', 0),
(175182, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'From the earth we come, and to the earth we return. Everything we have borrowed from it, we eventually give back.$B$BFrom the humblest dwarf to the most powerful lord; it is what we all have in common. No matter how rich or noble, in the end, we are naught but stone softened into flesh.', 0),
(175199, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hm... What do we have here?$B$B<Beldred inspects the ore beneath the shadow of her very long nose.>$B$BThe magic emanating from these stones feels familiar.$B$BGive me everything you found, and from now on, keep away from this ore.$B$BAssuming you wish to preserve what little sanity you display by asking me for help...$B$B<A shrill laugh escapes her.>', 0),
(175206, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<The elf takes the cheese assortment carefully, studying it for a moment before giving you a slight nod.>$B$BThis must be the cheesemaker''s apprentice''s order... At last. In Stormwind, even simple errands test the patience of someone who has lived for centuries.$B$B<She delicately takes a small piece of cheese and tastes it in silence, considering it calmly.>$B$BNot bad. But once you have tasted Windswept cheese, nothing else is quite the same. The Trias family is in serious trouble...', 0);
